        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 东南",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "东南 — dōngnán — \"southeast\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "huǒchēzhàn zài jīchǎng de dōngnán fāngxiàng — The railway station is southeast of the airport."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 南 (nán) — nine strokes: 十 on top; under it a frame open at the foot, a vertical down the left and a bar that turns down the right side and hooks; inside it a dot and a short stroke falling to the left, two bars, and a vertical down through them. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "东南 (dōngnán) is built from 东 'east' and 南 (nán) 'south', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tuwng and nom (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second as the direction of fire."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
